{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 1300,
    "dDurationMs": 3510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I recently received this question via email:\nHello there,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4810,
    "dDurationMs": 4830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Imagine we build a giant ring around the whole\nglobe, perfectly round, no ups and downs."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 9640,
    "dDurationMs": 4430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What you didn't know is that i installed explosives\nall around on each pole holding it up, and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 14070,
    "dDurationMs": 1080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then boom."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15150,
    "dDurationMs": 1780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All the poles break at the same time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16930,
    "dDurationMs": 1329,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What will happen to the ring?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 18259,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Will it just sit there in the air?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 19619,
    "dDurationMs": 1541,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or will it fall down?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21160,
    "dDurationMs": 1859,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Will it start spinning like crazy?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 23019,
    "dDurationMs": 2211,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Best regards, Martin from Sweden."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 25230,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First off, Martin, that was sneaky."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 26970,
    "dDurationMs": 4629,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I cannot condone secretly installing explosives\non poles holding up infrastructure projects."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 31599,
    "dDurationMs": 3561,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Second, I have a feeling you might really\nlike the planet Saturn."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35160,
    "dDurationMs": 2329,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And Third, fun question!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 37489,
    "dDurationMs": 3910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The answer depends a lot on how strong the\nring is, but in general you've touched upon"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41399,
    "dDurationMs": 1910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "an idea called symmetry breaking."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 43309,
    "dDurationMs": 4041,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As you've realized, a perfectly symmetric\nring doesn't have any particular reason to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 47350,
    "dDurationMs": 2090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fall or break in any one point!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 49440,
    "dDurationMs": 2630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Like a perfectly balanced pencil, which way\nwill it fall?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 52070,
    "dDurationMs": 3870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Anyway, if the ring is really really strong,\nthen it should just stay exactly where it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 55940,
    "dDurationMs": 3910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is, \"hovering\", though that actually means\nbeing held up by its own strength, because"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 59850,
    "dDurationMs": 4180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "each part will be gravitationally pulled toward\nthe center of the earth, and since those forces"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 64030,
    "dDurationMs": 3330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are spread equally around the ring in a symmetric\nway they’ll cancel out."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 67360,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Like how in tug of war if both sides pull\nthe same amount the rope won’t move)."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 71260,
    "dDurationMs": 4540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, if the ring’s not sufficiently strong,\nit might buckle in places and become scrunched"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 75800,
    "dDurationMs": 3930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "up, like the coins that my friend Dianna shrunk\nby putting them in a very strong, very quickly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 79730,
    "dDurationMs": 1460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "changing magnetic field."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81190,
    "dDurationMs": 3341,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It’s interesting to note that the properties\nof circumferences mean you’d only have to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 84531,
    "dDurationMs": 3899,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "take out a few meters for the ring to be small\nenough to just lie on the ground."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88430,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As for “will it start spinning like crazy”?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 90470,
    "dDurationMs": 4250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I think you might be referring to the idea\nthat the earth is spinning to the east “underneath”"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 94720,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the ring – well, I have a whole other video\nabout that, that you should definitely check"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 100080,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "out."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 101080,
    "dDurationMs": 34950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thanks for your question, and stay away from"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 136030,
    "dDurationMs": 7110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the high explosives."
    } ]
  } ]
}
